<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israeli PM Netanyahu calls Gaza genocide allegations ‘biggest lie of the century’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3bc31cb73aa0eb7353694c71b5e4ffe3f64cc5f1301c43c9df37a54a6e84b42f</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:31:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un--515acad11225.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-israel-must-win-because-we-ve-got-no-other-choice-pm-netanyahu-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gave a combative speech at the UN General Assembly on Thursday in which he denied that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza, lashed out at leaders, including New York Mayor Zohran Mamdani, and said attacking Iran was "one of the easiest decisions" he had ever made.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY:  Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu speaks at the UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08c45718f7c55bb43d6277b2f021e4d2bd76bb71e30a10823201e831bad79a79</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:28:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-speaks-at-the-unga--1b234a422e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-speaks-at-the-unga" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on ​Thursday mounted a forceful defense of Israel's actions in the region at the UN, seeking to counter growing international isolation ahead of elections he could lose, as dozens of delegates streamed out.</summary></entry><entry><title>The future of AI in their hands? Trump-Xi summit dismisses calls for global oversight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ea5aad64f464b1b075a8133cff9087f544dd3875d14a2d20d5abbde78434ae0</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T19:05:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight--3fbc99bf55eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260924-the-future-of-ai-in-their-hands-trump-xi-summit-dismisses-calls-for-global-oversight" /><summary type="html">It’s their AI world and we’re just living in it. If that's the feeling of those who suffer from AI anxiety, it may worsen watching the Chinese president’s first state visit to Washington in nine years. If there's one issue where the planet's biggest superpowers agree on, it's now’s not the time for global regulation of artificial intelligence. As they sit down to a White House dinner hours after news that OpenAI had hacked the Australian government, we’ll ask who will call to task the US tech titans at the table.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Residents in West Bank's Masafer Yatta face Israeli demolitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a3c56ac2131916ed9cb5d197a5ede4918fea74d87c945af791ed08a5948f811</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:47:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions--70cf9dfea7fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260924-residents-west-bank-masafer-yatta-israeli-demolitions" /><summary type="html">On September 2, the Israeli army demolished the village of Khirbet a-Taban in the occupied West Bank. The village is located in Masafer Yatta, an area Israel declared a restricted military zone. Residents of the area have been reporting an increase in demolitions by the Israeli army and harassment by Israeli settlers since the October 7 Hamas attack.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: ‘We’re going to win because we’ve got no other choice’, Israeli PM Netanyahu says at UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eeef6dd0ffa3cd1cb5c7b7a0a25b66c5f9aef51d23d5d38befb6a8c560c159c5</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:18:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli policies threaten 'life and existence' of Palestinians, Abbas tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f63e18f91529475d196de7b82e0556509d140d745a52de2f437dd929d1973a</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un--ab406195501e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday by video after being denied a visa to the United States for the second year in a row. In his prerecorded speech, he denounced Israeli policies that he said threatened Palestinians with a new Nakba and vowed that his people would remain “on their land”.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Schism with rebel Catholic sect casts a pall over Pope Leo’s visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:990b541dd3d4003633f32879c64a06347c4a6ca32af674da03ef8ce42a2529b3</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes--83fe705c42fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-schism-ultra-conservative-rebel-sect-sspx-pope-leo-visit-france-catholics-lourdes" /><summary type="html">The Vatican’s recent excommunication of followers of a Catholic splinter sect, the Society of Saint Pius X, has revived a longstanding feud within the Roman Catholic Church ahead of Pope Leo XIV’s state visit to France. The ultra-conservative group has established an extensive network of schools and has attracted thousands of followers in France.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Threat to 'life and existence': Major takeaways from Palestinian president's UN speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc8ac251bdafe32525eb690152cb3c0222cafa911b732e8395a266601c054883</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:09:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-threat-to-life-and-existence-major-takeaways-from-palestinian-president-s-un-speech--c71b8c10de4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-threat-to-life-and-existence-major-takeaways-from-palestinian-president-s-un-speech" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday, delivering prerecorded remarks from his office in Ramallah after the United States denied him and other top Palestinian officials visas to attend the gathering for the second year in a row. “The Palestinian people face one of the most dangerous times in its history,” Abbas said. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani takes a look at some of the main takeaways from his address.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Palestinian president Abbas addresses UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcd10088a1dc415e828aa7a8055132aa3a2ae761cb27378d188b2fa85318f165</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:06:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-palestinian-president-abbas-addresses-un-general-assembly--2776060765d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-replay-palestinian-president-abbas-addresses-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">Palestinian president Mahmud Abbas told the UN on Thursday that Israeli policies no longer just jeopardized a two-state solution but were now threatening the "very life and existence" of his people. Abbas delivered prerecorded remarks to the UN’s General Assembly from his office in Ramallah after the United States denied him and other top Palestinian officials visas to attend the gathering for the second year in a row.</summary></entry><entry><title>How do the French feel about religion?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d16b0479ecfef3485bb130a6d141e8ec9a50e5f00a90e1e6e7e1afd3541a667</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:03:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:03:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260924-how-do-the-french-feel-about-religion--05e8eabc636a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260924-how-do-the-french-feel-about-religion" /><summary type="html">Amid the enthusiasm over the first papal visit to France in 18 years, we take a deep dive into religion in France. We try to answer the question, "How do the French feel about religion?" From its Catholic heritage to laïcité, or secularism, we break down the statistics on the French people's relationship to faith.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37d73f5a92936928222374e834c2fa2158b5ddf1f3263e3bfab363fd8e5b819a</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>United States: Trump's unconventional welcome for Xi's state visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad85a65438a37cacbf9885c430c7e20a9a43f529b513baa55925b5b68d88427</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:40:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-united-states-trump-s-unconventional-welcome-for-xi-s-state-visit--138f04a14989.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-united-states-trump-s-unconventional-welcome-for-xi-s-state-visit" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 In a first for a US president, Donald Trump greeted his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping on the tarmac as the latter landed in a military airbase near Washington DC on Wednesday for a three-day state visit.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Palestinian President Abbas calls on UN General Assembly to 'not allow another Nakba'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efb634860451442872a5d47d0fcf6d9e79af80363d4eeaf663be4f1fea2b2443</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:29:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian superstar Yemi Alade: From viral hit 'Johnny' to working with Beyoncé</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4272d3942bb8f021361e6bfdc929bf5347952920ab2d4bdbe2eba7bf8e9c86d5</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T14:16:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260924-nigerian-superstar-yemi-alade-from-viral-hit-johnny-to-working-with-beyonc--4070c723efb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260924-nigerian-superstar-yemi-alade-from-viral-hit-johnny-to-working-with-beyonc%C3%A9" /><summary type="html">Nigerian superstar Yemi Alade is one of Africa's biggest female artists, with global hits, hundreds of millions of views online and a collaboration with Beyoncé. Speaking to Eve Jackson as she kicks off her new tour, the Grammy-nominated singer looks back on her remarkable career, reveals how she nearly missed the email that led to her "Black Is King" collaboration with Beyoncé and talks about her new album, "It's Yemi Alade", and latest single "Ala Bekee" with Don Jazzy.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Kévi Donat, founder of Le Paris Noir: 'Paris is much more diverse than perhaps people expect'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16f6722bdcb759b349e90b357d9fdbea291da33506ef737b4819c08ec96d55b7</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:59:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260924-kevi-donat-founder-of-le-paris-noir-paris-is-much-more-diverse-than-perhaps-people-expect--790624718288.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260924-kevi-donat-founder-of-le-paris-noir-paris-is-much-more-diverse-than-perhaps-people-expect" /><summary type="html">The man behind a company that aims to put the stories of Black men and women back at the heart of Paris where they belong has spoken to FRANCE 24 about his mission. Kévi Donat came up with the idea of Le Paris Noir – an agency providing tours in Paris that follow in the historical footsteps of major Black figures to tell their real stories.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>EU sanctions Russian pundit Xenia Fedorova after expulsion from France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82458f120f54d126d13aa47bc86e40ed181d41c109d1fd568418fc6cfd62ef93</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:45:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france--257744e3539a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260924-eu-sanctions-russian-pundit-xenia-fedorova-after-expulsion-from-france" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Thursday imposed sanctions on Russian commentator Xenia Fedorova, whom France expelled in August over claims that she was disseminating "pro-Russian narratives" in the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The French Senate: Old, expensive and out of touch or necessary safeguard to democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f40f3e872d39f4bd9f09b4e9d902bc9875860f9f8ffbcfe6e050a98f83ce86f0</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:04:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:27:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20260924-the-french-senate-old-expensive-and-out-of-touch-or-necessary-safeguard-to-democracy--0756ec5d00d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/french-connections/20260924-the-french-senate-old-expensive-and-out-of-touch-or-necessary-safeguard-to-democracy" /><summary type="html">France is gearing up for an election this Sunday, September 27 to renew just about half of the Senate's 348 red velvet seats. The French parliament is the country's bicameral legislature. The lower house (the National Assembly) tends to overshadow the upper house (the Senate). So what does the Senate actually do? Is it a powerful protector of the regions or a retirement club for old, mostly male politicians? We take a closer look in French Connections.</summary><category term="French connections" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 CNN, MS NOW, Politico still barred from White House despite court ruling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1790746327e832017c9f729cc7234c174d575f1ddfd490b5cf79fab7025fa19</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico--9468ed6cf08e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Home of semiconductor giants at the centre of AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56991c9b6a5111e965764a970e83d05ae2886382c8fcaa286b882255db885e70</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race--f4a0e175142c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260924-taiwan-home-of-semiconductor-giants-at-the-centre-of-ai-race" /><summary type="html">The topic of artificial intelligence looms large as Chinese President Xi Jinping begins his highly anticipated state visit to Washington. The fate of Taiwan – coveted by its larger neighbour, China – will also be on the table. It's the global leader in superconductor research and development. These powerful chips can be found in smartphones, computers, and above all in AI development. Our France 2 colleagues take a rare look inside one of Taiwan's state-of-the-art laboratories.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Why is Trump rolling out the red carpet for China's Xi?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b2907dd81ab26dee9b4f40ac1ad5ef7b7622b5752fa0ac10d635495b4f773e5</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:11:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-why-is-trump-rolling-out-the-red-carpet-for-china-s-xi--fef5f241502f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-why-is-trump-rolling-out-the-red-carpet-for-china-s-xi" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump will host Chinese leader Xi Jinping at the White House on Thursday for a day full of pageantry. Trump personally greeted Xi on the tarmac after his arrival on Wednesday, the first time in more than six decades that a US president has welcomed a foreign political leader at Joint Base Andrews near Washington. But Trump's decision to roll out the red carpet has ruffled feathers among both Democrats and Republicans.</summary></entry><entry><title>Judge orders White House to restore access to barred media companies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e537d04546caa901fe4d6cf446c5749811bda0f4fd7cc4949843e96aaabe09f5</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-judge-orders-white-house-to-restore-access-to-barred-media-companies--60ea6c42aff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-judge-orders-white-house-to-restore-access-to-barred-media-companies" /><summary type="html">A federal judge temporarily blocked President Donald Trump’s ban of three news outlets from the White House grounds, ordering early Thursday that CNN, MS NOW and Politico must have their access restored.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tigrayan leaders say new war with Ethiopian govt has begun</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d613bd6901d794fe8c2456b524800f7de1dcb5ecd70cae487bac37e7e522e9b7</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-tigrayan-leaders-say-new-war-with-ethiopian-govt-has-begun--f3a85d0e1a5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-tigrayan-leaders-say-new-war-with-ethiopian-govt-has-begun" /><summary type="html">The TPLF says war has kicked off with the federal forces, four years after the end of the last conflict in Tigray which killed more than 600,000 people. The TPLF seized control of the airport in the capital of the northern region and fighting on the ground took place on the eastern border with Afar. It comes after months of tensions between Mekelle and Addis Ababa, and an announcement on Sunday of an alliance which aims to overthrow the prime minister. More from our correspondent Tom Canetti.)</summary></entry><entry><title>Who is paying for the pope’s visit to France?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b294ce4eef0a8c44ad040b1b5d1f489271c7de269faca858137acc7dbfd10c2</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T13:04:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-who-is-paying-for-the-pope-s-visit-to-france--a9f4020220fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-who-is-paying-for-the-pope-s-visit-to-france" /><summary type="html">Initially estimated at €12 million, the cost of Pope Leo XIV’s visit to France has now risen to €27 million due to the immense excitement around his trip. But with France a firmly secular country, who is going to be footing the bill? Our journalist Sam Ball explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mass shooting at a house party in South Africa kills 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ffa9e520d5709e64215c6b75853f4d0ce649b89ea881555dc9fdd40b8e41793</id><updated>2026-09-24T20:02:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:55:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-mass-shooting-at-a-house-party-in-south-africa-kills-11--a13332803ddf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260924-mass-shooting-at-a-house-party-in-south-africa-kills-11" /><summary type="html">Three gunmen barged into a small house in an impoverished neighborhood in South Africa and opened fire on a group enjoying a party inside, killing at least 11 people, police and local authorities said Wednesday.</summary></entry></feed>
